], "date": 1503928900, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "7279": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1387918 - Retrieve current array for owner in aria owns hash table. r=surkov, a=jcristau", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "32eec29a85a507a83f1f4f875aa2c94ca6910647", "parents": ["e45e2146178462a5f21f95e8b0630fd76ce036e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1373222 - MutableBlobStorage always returns a temporary-file Blob if the size of data is greater than 1mb. r=smaug, a=jcristau", "files": ["dom/base/MutableBlobStorage.cpp", "dom/base/MutableBlobStorage.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ecef71fa933fe1a0334060a98103e59d44c6c7ef", "parents": ["32eec29a85a507a83f1f4f875aa2c94ca6910647"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Francois Marier \u003cfrancois@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1376036 - Run data and blob URIs through Application Reputation checks. r=gcp, a=jcristau\n\nblob URIs are sent through unfiltered and data URIs are hashed in\nthe same way as Chrome does.\n\nAlso, we used to bail on the first invalid URL we encountered. We now\nkeep going, checking the other URLs in the chain and eventually doing\nthe remote lookup.", "files": ["toolkit/components/downloads/ApplicationReputation.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "68a444daf85b7b5a11bca63424d878b8e6a84fb2", "parents": ["ecef71fa933fe1a0334060a98103e59d44c6c7ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1376825 - Set eIsNotInDocument to accessible's state when unbinding from doc. r=surkov, a=jcristau", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "eeeec9cafc4ed60652c26f5a3df905ae6bce5946", "parents": ["68a444daf85b7b5a11bca63424d878b8e6a84fb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1385272 - Make plaintext serializer not crash when a \u003ctr\u003e is a child of a \u003ctr\u003e. r=Ehsan, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: CMNIWYX8R07", "files": ["dom/base/crashtests/1385272-1.html", "dom/base/crashtests/crashtests.list", "dom/base/nsDocumentEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d68fa12fbffc0cee419f920fac12a7c8cb6b2be7", "parents": ["eeeec9cafc4ed60652c26f5a3df905ae6bce5946"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Chang \u003cmchang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1390002 - There are some paths to find out if dwrite is enabled, which inits gfxPlatform, which requires information from PopulateScreenInfo, which depends on the refresh driver existing. At this time however, we haven't initialized our vsync source so we crash. This moves vsync initialization earlier in the gfx pipeline. r=kats, a=jcristau", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c24e6fc9f689aeb32de0bf7916b1d0098d4a2bb9", "parents": ["d68fa12fbffc0cee419f920fac12a7c8cb6b2be7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cphilip.chimento@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1379539 - Remove unnecessary NSPR dependency. r=glandium, a=jcristau", "files": ["build/autoconf/nspr-build.m4", "js/src/js.pc.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5d95b2833b30582ab3df4e28373d749ddbf7c04e", "parents": ["c24e6fc9f689aeb32de0bf7916b1d0098d4a2bb9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1503935723, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "7280": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug, Automated HSTS preload list update from host bld-linux64-spot-302 - a=hsts-update", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.errors", "sec